.docname {Plugin Package Format}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

BakingRL v2 packages are described by `bakingrl.plugin.json`.

## Minimal Manifest

```json
{
  "schema": "bakingrl.plugin/2",
  "id": "com.example.my-package",
  "name": "My Package",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "exports": {
    "visuals": {
      "scoreboard": {
        "entry": "dist/visuals/scoreboard.js",
        "defaultSize": [760, 128],
        "settings": "schemas/scoreboard-settings.json"
      }
    },
    "layouts": {
      "stream": {
        "path": "templates/stream-layout.json",
        "title": "Stream Layout"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Export Types

- `exports.visuals`: browser ESM modules mounted in overlays and pages.
- `exports.components`: reusable visual components loaded by visuals.
- `exports.services`: sandboxed backend modules with callable methods.
- `exports.connectors`: backend modules with explicit network permissions.
- `exports.pages`: importable page templates.
- `exports.layouts`: importable overlay layout templates.

## Visual Instance Settings

`exports.visuals.<name>.settings` can point to a JSON Schema file. BakingRL uses
that schema to render typed instance settings in the page and layout editors,
instead of forcing users to edit raw JSON.

Settings schemas should be JSON Schema objects with `properties`. Use
`title`, `description`, `default`, `required`, numeric/string bounds, and
primitive option lists to make the generated editor form readable.

Supported field shapes in the current host UI:

- `type: "string"`, including `format: "color"`;
- `type: "number"` or `type: "integer"`;
- `type: "boolean"`;
- `enum`, `oneOf`, or `anyOf` options with primitive values;
- `type: "array"` with primitive options declared on `items`.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "title": "Scoreboard Settings",
  "properties": {
    "accent": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "color",
      "default": "#38bdf8"
    },
    "showBoost": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": true
    },
    "density": {
      "type": "string",
      "default": "comfortable",
      "oneOf": [
        { "const": "compact", "title": "Compact" },
        { "const": "comfortable", "title": "Comfortable" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Page Templates

`exports.pages` contains templates for host-owned page layouts. Importing a
template does not create a plugin-owned route or window. BakingRL assigns fresh
IDs and timestamps, tracks template provenance, and then lets users edit the
page like any other page.

## Layout Templates

`exports.layouts` contains templates for overlay layouts. A template is
imported into BakingRL's host-owned layout list; it does not create an overlay
runtime by itself. Users can then route the imported layout to the in-game
overlay or OBS stream output.

Layout template IDs, layer IDs, item IDs, timestamps, and template provenance
may be rewritten during import. Keep portable behavior in package/export
references and item settings rather than relying on template IDs.

## Distribution Bundle

The `.brlp` format is a ZIP archive. Required:

```txt
bakingrl.plugin.json
```

Supported:

```txt
dist/
assets/
schemas/
templates/
manifest.hashes.json
signature.ed25519
```

The helper CLI can generate hashes, signatures, and `.brlp` archives.

```sh
npm run pack
npm run keygen -- signing-key.json
npm run pack -- --sign signing-key.json
```

## Versioning

Use semantic versions in package manifests. BakingRL treats package IDs as
stable identities, so avoid changing an ID after publishing.
